      "writtenOn": "2026-09-11T07:45:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We are missing also some important differences between JGit and C-Git in terms of packing logic:\n\n1. C-Git creates packfiles regardless of their objects pointing to a specific namespace. JGit instead have one packfiles for heads/tags and another for everything else\n2. C-Git generates multi-pack bitmaps that JGit and Gerrit cannot understand\n3. C-Git won\u0027t be able to be resilient to NFS stale handles\n\nWouldn\u0027t be easier to just use JGit instead, or at least making it configurable?\nI see the `git gc` hardcoded in these scripts.",
      "revId": "813aa842dc8838bdfdb076b888be97b6fd6742ff",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
